course: dictionary
lesson: 10097
title: Thickness: three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Thickness is a noun, and it can mean more than one thing. It can mean how thick something is, how runny or dense it is, or a layer of something. The rest of the sentence tells you which meaning is meant.
explain: «Measure the thickness of the book» means the distance from one side of the book to the other, through the pages. In maths and science lessons, thickness is often measured in millimetres or centimetres.
explain: In cooking, thickness tells you how runny a sauce is. A thick sauce pours slowly. Thickness of ice also matters for safety on a frozen pond, so always check the meaning against the sentence before you decide.
fact: Thickness means how thick something is, from one side to the other.
fact: Thickness can also mean how dense or runny something is, like a liquid or fog.
fact: A thickness is a layer of something.
fact: «Real silk of Spider-Man's thickness could not stop a train, but silk is very good at soaking up energy by stretching.» Here the sentence is about how thick the silk is, and it says silk soaks up energy by stretching.
fact: Useful phrases: «a thickness of» (a layer of something) and «measure the thickness» (find out how thick something is).
exercise: «Measure the thickness of the book.» What does thickness mean here? | The colour of the cover | *The distance from one side to the other | The weight of the pages | How runny it is
exercise: The cook checked the thickness of the sauce. What does thickness mean here? | The number of spoons used | The price of the sauce | *How runny or dense it is | The distance across the pan
exercise: «A thickness of ice covered the pond.» What does a thickness of mean here? | *A layer of | A kind of skating on | A very cold day on | The depth of the water under
test: What does thickness mean in «the thickness of the book»? | Its weight in grams | *The distance from one side to the other | Its colour | A kind of thick paper
test: Which meaning fits «The thickness of the fog hid the road»? | How far it is across | A layer of paint | Its smell | *How dense it is
exam: Mia says thickness only means how thick something is. Is she right? | Yes, and it is always measured in litres | No, it means how fast something moves | *No, it can also mean how dense or runny something is, or a layer of something | Yes, that is the only meaning
